          <h2>First 30 Seconds Safety Checklist</h2>

          <p>
            Before continuing a random video call, quickly ask yourself the following questions:
          </p>

          <h3>Before You Answer</h3>

          <ul>
            <li>✅ Is my camera positioned comfortably?</li>
            <li>✅ Is my background free from sensitive personal information?</li>
            <li>✅ Is my microphone working properly?</li>
            <li>✅ Am I using a trusted platform?</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>During the First 30 Seconds</h3>

          <ul>
            <li>✅ Did the other person greet me respectfully?</li>
            <li>✅ Are they asking normal conversation starters instead of personal questions?</li>
            <li>✅ Do they seem patient rather than rushing the interaction?</li>
            <li>✅ Are they comfortable staying on the platform?</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>If Something Feels Wrong</h3>

          <ul>
            <li>✅ End the conversation politely.</li>
            <li>✅ Do not share your phone number or social media immediately.</li>
            <li>✅ Never send money or financial information.</li>
            <li>✅ Report suspicious users if the platform provides reporting tools.</li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            These simple habits take less than a minute but significantly reduce the likelihood of continuing conversations that may become uncomfortable or unsafe.
          </p>


